# Day 17: local build snapshot used for Lighthouse runs
Day17/verification/dist-snapshot.tgz

# Environment files. Real values never get committed -- only the .env.example
# template does. See Day17/.env.example for what belongs where, and note that
# the two actual secrets in this project deliberately do NOT live in a .env:
# the SWA deployment token lives in GitHub Actions secrets, and Jwt:Secret
# lives in dotnet user-secrets (see the README).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.template

# Azure Functions local config -- holds whatever you put in it, so it is
# ignored and only the .example is tracked.
local.settings.json

# Day 17 BFF build output
Day17/api-bff/publish/
Day17/api-bff/deploy.zip

# Day 22 -- the API's own console from prove-circuit.ps1. Written on every run
# and useful while diagnosing a run that will not start, but it is EF Core
# Debug noise at ~360KB a time: 'Closing data reader' lines are weight, not
# evidence. The resilience-relevant lines are extracted into
# day22-api-resilience-lines.txt, which is committed.
Day22/verification/day22-api-stdout.log
Day22/verification/day22-api-stderr.log

# azd environment state. azd writes its own .azure/.gitignore containing '*',
# so this is belt-and-braces rather than the only guard -- but that nested file
# is azd's to rewrite, and infra/main.bicep's output comments assume .azure is
# NOT ignored here (which is why no connection string is emitted as a template
# output). Making it true at the root as well costs one line.
.azure/

# The Claude desktop app mirrors delivered files into this folder inside the
# connected workspace. They are duplicates of files that already live at their
# real paths; committing them would give every deliverable two homes that drift.
Claude outputs/
